-- PAPER-LEARN-PROBATION-SETTLE-1 part 4 of 9 (2026-11-05, charter pillar autonomy, program QNFO.OPS; cluster C8-PROJECTS-GOALS of the roadmap and backlog completion sweep).
-- Settles 25 probationary direct paper learnings (ids 4927 to 5066 of the 225 read on 2026-11-04 23:00Z): each row was read in full (claim, lever, application and the model's apply signal) against the live fleet and given one disposition with its reason.
-- PAPER-LEARN-TRIAGE-1 parked them in probation because its catalogue held 6 mechanisms; the apply signal usually meant the model did not know the fleet already does this. Dispositions: already-in-place (mechanism named, existence read today), rejected (category and specific reason, with what would justify re-proposing), routed (to agent_issues 1000459 TRIGGER-FLAP-1 or goal external-impact-per-dollar).
-- Each goal PAPER-LEARN-<id> (DoD: the learning is settled) then completes on its next probe, and roadmap row GL-PAPER-LEARN-<id> verifies in the hourly loop. Revert one row: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'probation' WHERE id = <id>.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = (SELECT b.fleet_status FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_04 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), status_note = (SELECT b.status_note FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_04 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id), updated_at = (SELECT b.updated_at FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_04 b WHERE b.id = paper_learnings.id) WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM bak_20261105_c8_pl_04)

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261105_c8_pl_04 AS SELECT * FROM paper_learnings WHERE id IN (4927, 4929, 4935, 4936, 4937, 4938, 4939, 4941, 4962, 4964, 4965, 4971, 4972, 4973, 4974, 4976, 4977, 5009, 5010, 5015, 5019, 5030, 5034, 5064, 5066);

UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; modeleval): The strongest realistic challenger is the production control: qnfo-model-eval benchmarks each candidate against it on a fixed battery and reverts on a quality drop.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4927 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; pred): Fleet-authored changes already carry metric, baseline and prediction: pull request descriptions name the roadmap row, charter pillar and prediction, and decision_log.predicted_outcome is logged for 98 percent of decisions (prediction_logged_share_7d 0.983 read 2026-11-04T23:04Z).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4929 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; birth,sla): An issue is born with a closing probe and a deadline: QUEUE-SLA-1 and SLA-120M-1 bound every item at 120 minutes with an escalation, and an expired issue is acted on, not extended (issues_open_over_120m, v_issue_age_ladder).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4935 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; independent): Verification is already routed away from the producer: probes run in qnfo-fleet-control and the consumer, the review gate uses two disjoint families that did not write the diff, and the stale-PR lane merges.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4936 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'routed', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 routed (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; goal-cost): Routed to goal external-impact-per-dollar (qnfo-fleet-control, adopted, program QNFO.OPS): a normalized cost per verified solution is the standing cost-per-outcome goal. Tracked there with a machine check written by the 2026-11-05 roadmap sweep.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4937 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; merge): Verification runs inside the merge cycle: pr-checks, PR-FAST-GUARDS-1, the REVIEW-GATE-1 read and the DEPLOY-PROBES-1 canary revert gate a pull request before and just after it deploys.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4938 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): The fleet already records and publishes its own refutations (prediction_miss_rate_7d 0.26, the errata pipeline for its papers); crediting well-designed falsifications in the trust ledger would add a scoring rule with no measured case of a loop avoiding a falsification. Re-propose with such a case.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4939 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; pred,birth): Forecasts carry a deadline and a refutation: a prediction is logged before the change and compared after, an issue is born with its closing probe, and a missed SLA files its own issue (sla_breaches_over_120m).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4941 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; unmeasured): A metric with no numeric value cannot pass silently as healthy: v_metric_trigger_state returns hit NULL (unmeasured), not false, when the value is not a number, and the guard metrics_unmeasured counts those triggers (14 read 2026-11-04T22:42Z, matching the 14 NULL-valued triggers listed from the view).', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4962 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): Catastrophic cancellation is a floating-point fact; fleet metrics are SQL counts, ratios and windowed sums over rows, and no breach is shown to come from subtracting two near-equal cumulative totals. Re-propose with a metric whose delta lost its significant digits.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4964 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Absorption in a running float total is not what broke the fleet''s cost rollups: the measured discrepancies were pricing and coverage bugs (the spend ledger priced @cf gateway models at the wrong rate, fixed in PR 6985), and costs are summed from per-call rows in SQL. Re-propose with a rollup whose total disagrees with its rows.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4965 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; modeleval): Cheap-first with escalation on evidence exists: COST-CUT-CODE-1 (#7247) orders the code loop''s model rungs cheap first, stops on a patch that is too large and caps output on the dear rung; BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1 steers to the cheapest capable model.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4971 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; governance): Rule amendment is separated from rule execution: CLAUDE.md, the charter and the doctrine change only by pull request through the canonical path (governance changes land by PR, RULE-8-RETIRED-1), and a loop cannot amend them while it runs.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4972 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; analogy-only): Complementary chemical and electrical signalling is a biological analogy. The fleet already runs separate channels by timescale (5-minute dispatcher, hourly metric tick, daily loops, work claims for targeted signals) and no crosstalk between them is shown.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4973 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; spof): Redundancy on critical paths is a standing rule and a ledger: ANTIFRAGILE-1 requires a design with one executor, model or transport on a critical path to ship with its second path or an issue that builds it, and spof_registry records each single point of failure.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4974 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Continuous convex re-balancing across model tiers would replace BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1 (steer to the cheapest capable model at a cap) with an optimizer; no measured loss from the current rule is shown. Re-propose with a cost or quality gap that the cap rule leaves.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4976 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; selfchange): Self-modification is already scoped and benchmarked: the code loop changes its own and control-plane code behind a functional canary with automatic revert (CODE-LOOP-CONTROL-PLANE-1, CM_LOOP_CANARIED), deploy probes baseline each worker and revert a regression, and each worker''s suites run on every pull request.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 4977 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; pred): Acceptance thresholds are committed before execution: a change states its predicted metric, direction and size in the pull request and decision_log.predicted_outcome (prediction_logged_share_7d 0.983), and an issue''s closing probe is written at birth.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5009 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): The trust ledger credits verified outcomes read from live probes and measurements, not a loop''s own generated test data; no credit from self-generated data is shown. The tool-versus-hypothesis split is the paper''s statement about its synthetic data. Re-propose with a credit that rested on synthetic data.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5010 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Loop capacity is observed in production (per-run timing in the consumer and fleet_runs, D1 read volume tracked in the cold-tier work) and scope widening is limited to fleet loop scopes through the canonical path; no widening is shown to have outrun measured capacity. Re-propose with one.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5015 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'already-in-place', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 in place (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; premise): A stuck remedy questions its own premise: remediation_contracts.max_attempts parks an over-retried contract as escalated, METRIC-CLOSED-LOOP-1 replaces a remedy that did not move its metric within 7 days and allows a wrong target to be corrected with evidence, and blocker_redteam and belief_registry record false beliefs removed.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5019 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): A per-artifact aliasing or uncertainty score needs a calibrated signal the models do not give; the pipeline already records review-unresolved and verify events per paper and holds claims by CLAIM-INTEGRITY-1. Re-propose with a calibrated uncertainty measure that predicts later corrections.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5030 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Loops already differ in tolerance by construction: code merges pass pr-checks, the review gate and canary revert, pipeline papers pass the reviewer, verify and claim-integrity stages, and outreach follows consent rules; no loop is shown to have the wrong tolerance. Re-propose with a measured over- or under-strict loop.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5034 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'routed', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 routed (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; trigger-flap): Routed to agent_issues 1000459 (TRIGGER-FLAP-1, open, critical, qnfo-fleet-control): requiring more than one observation before a trigger files an issue (a band and a minimum run of breaches) is the fix that issue measures against 167 reopens on 44 tickets in 7 days.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5064 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
UPDATE paper_learnings SET fleet_status = 'rejected', status_note = 'PL-TRIAGE-2 rejected (c8-projects-goals session, 2026-11-05; no-measured-gap): Extrapolation from few cycles is already checked after the fact: predictions are logged before a change and compared with the re-measured value (prediction_miss_rate_7d 0.26). Re-propose with a steady-state forecast that failed because too few cycles were fitted.', updated_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now') WHERE id = 5066 AND fleet_status = 'probation';
